1
00:00:00,370 --> 00:00:01,910
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:01,970 --> 00:00:03,240
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,310 --> 00:00:05,210
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:06,980 --> 00:00:08,180
(Episode 6)

5
00:00:30,770 --> 00:00:31,970
There you are.

6
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:34,970
Hello. I'm the one
who contacted you...

7
00:00:45,880 --> 00:00:46,920
It's been a while.

8
00:00:47,620 --> 00:00:48,620
What are you doing here?

9
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:52,360
Where's Ms. Kim?
Why are you here instead?

10
00:00:52,460 --> 00:00:54,060
Because I'm the one
who asked you to come.

11
00:00:54,760 --> 00:00:55,830
Why?

12
00:00:56,060 --> 00:00:58,000
Did you think Kim Jung Sun
actually replied?

13
00:00:59,460 --> 00:01:00,730
How naive.

14
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:05,970
Are you going to keep trying
to stop me?

15
00:01:06,810 --> 00:01:09,270
Fine, just you try.

16
00:01:10,040 --> 00:01:11,740
Let's see how long
you can keep this up.

17
00:01:12,380 --> 00:01:14,080
I'm asking this of you
one last time.

18
00:01:15,710 --> 00:01:17,780
Keep that matter a secret.

19
00:01:19,050 --> 00:01:20,750
I already told you I won't.

20
00:01:21,050 --> 00:01:22,050
You...

21
00:01:23,290 --> 00:01:24,920
Are you sure you won't regret this?

22
00:01:25,820 --> 00:01:27,590
What? Regret?

23
00:01:28,490 --> 00:01:30,500
Hey, Park Hee Jung.

24
00:01:30,560 --> 00:01:31,760
Why do you keep saying my name?

25
00:01:45,080 --> 00:01:47,810
Why? Feeling dizzy?

26
00:01:51,350 --> 00:01:52,750
What do you think you're doing?

27
00:02:10,700 --> 00:02:12,240
(My Daughter)

28
00:02:12,300 --> 00:02:14,370
What did you just spray on me?

29
00:02:15,040 --> 00:02:16,070
See?

30
00:02:17,140 --> 00:02:19,480
You should've taken
this last chance.

31
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:25,250
All right.
I get it now, so just stop.

32
00:02:25,920 --> 00:02:28,520
I'll keep it a secret.

33
00:02:30,020 --> 00:02:31,260
Please, just stop.

34
00:02:33,460 --> 00:02:35,860
(Danger: Keep Out)

35
00:02:36,760 --> 00:02:37,760
No.

36
00:02:39,030 --> 00:02:40,400
It's too late now.

37
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:43,600
(Danger: Keep Out)

38
00:02:50,510 --> 00:02:51,510
(Danger: Keep Out)

39
00:03:12,730 --> 00:03:15,430
The person you are trying to reach
is unavailable.

40
00:04:29,710 --> 00:04:30,710
Mom.

41
00:04:31,410 --> 00:04:32,410
Mom?

42
00:04:52,400 --> 00:04:53,400
No...

43
00:04:56,770 --> 00:04:58,800
It can't be true. It can't be.

44
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:02,270
It can't be. No...

45
00:05:04,280 --> 00:05:06,310
Please, it can't be.

46
00:05:10,450 --> 00:05:11,450
No...

47
00:05:13,720 --> 00:05:14,720
No.

48
00:05:19,620 --> 00:05:22,630
No...

49
00:05:22,690 --> 00:05:26,660
No, it can't be.

50
00:05:27,070 --> 00:05:31,240
That can't be Mom. No way.

51
00:05:34,570 --> 00:05:35,610
That can't be Mom.

52
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:41,210
No... No way.

53
00:05:42,280 --> 00:05:44,720
Please, no.

54
00:05:46,250 --> 00:05:48,050
No...

55
00:05:54,790 --> 00:05:56,990
Mom!

56
00:06:00,300 --> 00:06:02,670
Somebody help me.

57
00:06:02,900 --> 00:06:05,040
Please, Mom...

58
00:06:05,470 --> 00:06:10,140
Oh no, what do I do? Mom!

59
00:06:12,310 --> 00:06:14,910
Somebody, please help!

60
00:06:17,120 --> 00:06:21,650
Oh no. Please, is anyone there?

61
00:06:25,960 --> 00:06:28,190
Mom, oh no!

62
00:06:28,630 --> 00:06:30,630
What's going on over there?
Is something wrong?

63
00:06:31,060 --> 00:06:32,460
Mom, no...

64
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:34,230
What do I do?

65
00:06:34,300 --> 00:06:36,500
- What's wrong?
- What do I do?

66
00:06:38,900 --> 00:06:40,070
What is it? What's wrong?

67
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:50,520
Hey, what happened?
They said you were there too.

68
00:06:51,920 --> 00:06:53,220
What on earth happened?

69
00:06:54,290 --> 00:06:56,690
Hey, Eun Seol. Ko Eun Seol!

70
00:06:57,050 --> 00:06:58,060
Eun Guk.

71
00:06:59,990 --> 00:07:01,290
Ask her later.

72
00:07:02,060 --> 00:07:03,390
She's having a tough time as it is.

73
00:07:24,050 --> 00:07:25,150
Who's Ko Eun Seol?

74
00:07:29,790 --> 00:07:31,290
Are you Ko Eun Seol?

75
00:07:32,160 --> 00:07:33,890
Yes, I am. Why?

76
00:07:34,430 --> 00:07:35,430
We're police officers.

77
00:07:35,930 --> 00:07:39,030
Ko Eun Seol, you're under arrest
for the murder of Park Hee Jung.

78
00:07:39,060 --> 00:07:40,130
Please come with us.

79
00:07:41,570 --> 00:07:43,800
- What?
- What did you just say?

80
00:07:43,970 --> 00:07:46,170
- Who murdered who?
- Let's head to the station.

81
00:07:46,300 --> 00:07:48,410
- But...
- What do you think you're doing?

82
00:07:48,710 --> 00:07:50,840
What could my daughter have done
for you to drag her away like this?

83
00:07:50,980 --> 00:07:53,110
It really wasn't me.
There must be some kind of mistake.

84
00:07:53,110 --> 00:07:54,780
- Let's go.
- Hey, wait a minute. Hold on.

85
00:07:54,780 --> 00:07:56,380
- Dad. Eun Guk.
- Wait!

86
00:07:57,520 --> 00:07:58,980
We'll now begin
questioning the witness.

87
00:08:01,150 --> 00:08:02,150
Lee Jung Tae.

88
00:08:03,020 --> 00:08:05,160
- Yes?
- You're a guard at Serim Tower...

89
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:06,660
and were the first
to report the fall.

90
00:08:07,330 --> 00:08:08,560
Yes, I'm the one who called it in.

91
00:08:08,590 --> 00:08:10,830
Then please tell us
exactly what you saw...

92
00:08:10,830 --> 00:08:11,900
on the rooftop that day.

93
00:08:11,960 --> 00:08:15,230
Sure. I was on shift that day,
doing my rounds...

94
00:08:16,170 --> 00:08:17,940
when I heard an argument.

95
00:08:18,170 --> 00:08:21,210
So I went to see what was going on,
and I saw...

96
00:08:23,570 --> 00:08:24,710
that student...

97
00:08:26,040 --> 00:08:29,810
push the victim over the railing.

98
00:08:35,450 --> 00:08:37,190
Objection.

99
00:08:37,890 --> 00:08:38,890
Witness.

100
00:08:39,390 --> 00:08:40,860
Then why is your testimony different
from your report?

101
00:08:41,530 --> 00:08:43,660
In your report,
you only said someone fell.

102
00:08:43,860 --> 00:08:46,060
You didn't say anyone pushed them.
Why is that?

103
00:08:46,130 --> 00:08:47,870
Well, that's because...

104
00:08:48,070 --> 00:08:51,340
I was so shocked and panicked
that I wasn't thinking straight.

105
00:08:52,070 --> 00:08:53,770
If you weren't thinking straight,

106
00:08:53,840 --> 00:08:55,640
wouldn't you have just reported
what you saw?

107
00:08:55,640 --> 00:08:58,040
And if that were true,

108
00:08:59,040 --> 00:09:00,280
why didn't you try to stop her?

109
00:09:00,810 --> 00:09:01,850
If you saw her pushing the victim,

110
00:09:01,910 --> 00:09:03,050
shouldn't you have tried
to stop her?

111
00:09:03,050 --> 00:09:05,780
She pushed her
before I even had a chance to intervene.

112
00:09:06,180 --> 00:09:07,320
That's not true.

113
00:09:07,450 --> 00:09:10,720
He's lying. It's a lie.

114
00:09:10,790 --> 00:09:12,460
I didn't push her.

115
00:09:13,360 --> 00:09:17,130
When I got there,
my mother had already fallen.

116
00:09:17,300 --> 00:09:19,560
He got there after me.

117
00:09:20,300 --> 00:09:22,830
Sir, why are you lying?

118
00:09:23,170 --> 00:09:24,870
Why are you doing this to me? Why?

119
00:09:24,870 --> 00:09:26,000
Order.

120
00:09:26,640 --> 00:09:27,910
Control yourself, defendant.

121
00:09:28,610 --> 00:09:30,810
One more outburst
and you'll be removed from the courtroom.

122
00:09:31,680 --> 00:09:32,680
Eun Seol, please.

123
00:09:33,580 --> 00:09:35,180
- Witness.
- Yes?

124
00:09:35,180 --> 00:09:37,420
Are you sure
you're telling the absolute truth?

125
00:09:37,480 --> 00:09:41,190
Yes, Your Honor. I saw it clearly
with my own two eyes.

126
00:09:41,390 --> 00:09:43,890
Besides, why would I lie?

127
00:09:44,320 --> 00:09:45,560
I have no reason to.

128
00:09:45,620 --> 00:09:46,920
(Prosecution)

129
00:09:46,990 --> 00:09:49,260
That's all for this witness.

130
00:09:50,030 --> 00:09:51,330
No.

131
00:09:51,830 --> 00:09:54,170
I didn't kill my mom.

132
00:09:54,400 --> 00:09:57,600
Why would I kill my own mom? Why?

133
00:09:58,470 --> 00:10:00,100
I really didn't kill her!

134
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:02,010
Bailiff, escort her out.

135
00:10:02,010 --> 00:10:03,870
Please, you have to believe me.

136
00:10:03,940 --> 00:10:06,380
It really wasn't me.

137
00:10:07,580 --> 00:10:10,050
Why would I kill my own mom? Why?

138
00:10:12,120 --> 00:10:13,120
Dad!

139
00:10:13,180 --> 00:10:15,490
Eun Seol... Eun Seol!

140
00:10:19,420 --> 00:10:22,590
- Hey, pretty face.
- Well, hello there.

141
00:10:22,860 --> 00:10:24,660
So what are you in for?

142
00:10:24,900 --> 00:10:27,400
- Not going to answer?
- We'll see you in the cell.

143
00:10:27,570 --> 00:10:29,170
Hey, welcome!

144
00:10:31,100 --> 00:10:32,470
The defendant, Ko Eun Seol,

145
00:10:32,800 --> 00:10:34,640
was indicted
on the charge of murder.

146
00:10:35,110 --> 00:10:38,680
Based on the witness testimony
and the evidence submitted,

147
00:10:39,040 --> 00:10:40,580
the court finds you guilty.

148
00:10:41,080 --> 00:10:44,050
You are hereby sentenced
to 15 years in prison.

149
00:10:52,360 --> 00:10:53,690
Hey, new girl.

150
00:10:55,860 --> 00:10:57,130
Why don't you introduce yourself?

151
00:10:58,300 --> 00:10:59,300
Go on.

152
00:10:59,660 --> 00:11:02,030
Hey. Are you deaf?

153
00:11:02,970 --> 00:11:04,840
The boss told you
to introduce yourself.

154
00:11:09,540 --> 00:11:10,810
Want me to kill you?

155
00:11:11,580 --> 00:11:13,780
What, you still
don't get the situation?

156
00:11:15,610 --> 00:11:16,610
Stab me.

157
00:11:20,450 --> 00:11:21,550
Please, stab me.

158
00:11:22,150 --> 00:11:23,290
What the...

159
00:11:29,060 --> 00:11:30,060
Why?

160
00:11:30,800 --> 00:11:31,800
Can't you do it?

161
00:11:31,860 --> 00:11:33,430
- What...
- I said stab me.

162
00:11:33,960 --> 00:11:34,970
- Why?
- Hold on.

163
00:11:34,970 --> 00:11:36,200
You can't do it?

164
00:11:36,670 --> 00:11:39,000
- I said stab me.
- Darn, what a nutjob.

165
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:40,910
Girls, she needs
to be taught a lesson.

166
00:11:41,010 --> 00:11:42,010
Get her!

167
00:11:58,760 --> 00:11:59,760
Hey.

168
00:12:00,620 --> 00:12:01,730
Come and eat.

169
00:12:02,590 --> 00:12:03,690
That little...

170
00:12:04,200 --> 00:12:06,160
Hey, leave her be.

171
00:12:07,830 --> 00:12:09,070
She's not in her right mind
right now.

172
00:12:10,030 --> 00:12:12,540
Mess with her now, and we might
end up with a dead body.

173
00:12:13,900 --> 00:12:15,640
Darn, I've lost my appetite.

174
00:12:28,220 --> 00:12:29,420
She's refusing visitors.

175
00:12:30,920 --> 00:12:31,920
Again?

176
00:12:32,890 --> 00:12:33,890
I understand.

177
00:12:35,490 --> 00:12:36,830
We have an emergency, ma'am.

178
00:12:36,830 --> 00:12:38,500
- What is it?
- Ko Eun Seol tried to harm herself.

179
00:12:38,500 --> 00:12:39,500
What?

180
00:12:39,930 --> 00:12:40,970
What was that?

181
00:12:48,570 --> 00:12:50,740
Eun Seol. Ms. Ko!

182
00:12:51,310 --> 00:12:52,880
Stay with me, Ms. Ko.

183
00:12:53,410 --> 00:12:54,410
Ms. Ko!

184
00:12:57,380 --> 00:12:59,780
(Surgery in Progress)

185
00:13:05,520 --> 00:13:06,620
What's her blood pressure?

186
00:13:07,220 --> 00:13:08,690
It's dropping to 80.

187
00:13:09,190 --> 00:13:10,330
What about the blood
for transfusion?

188
00:13:10,390 --> 00:13:12,400
We were notified
that she's A-negative,

189
00:13:12,460 --> 00:13:13,730
which we've already requested.

190
00:13:16,200 --> 00:13:17,500
Her blood pressure
is still dropping.

191
00:13:18,140 --> 00:13:20,170
Increase the fluids
and start another line.

192
00:13:20,240 --> 00:13:21,240
Got it.

193
00:13:33,480 --> 00:13:35,550
- The blood's here.
- Hook it up immediately.

194
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:52,600
Eun Seol.

195
00:14:13,420 --> 00:14:14,690
Stay strong, Eun Seol.

196
00:14:15,660 --> 00:14:16,790
You have to live.

197
00:14:18,530 --> 00:14:21,400
I'm with you, always.

198
00:14:36,510 --> 00:14:37,550
Mom...

199
00:14:41,250 --> 00:14:42,390
Mom...

200
00:14:44,820 --> 00:14:45,820
Mom...

201
00:14:47,460 --> 00:14:49,160
Mom, don't go.

202
00:14:49,360 --> 00:14:50,890
Doctor, she's responding.

203
00:14:51,030 --> 00:14:52,730
Ms. Ko, can you hear me?

204
00:14:53,260 --> 00:14:54,970
Mom, don't go.

205
00:14:57,600 --> 00:14:58,800
Don't go.

206
00:15:00,840 --> 00:15:01,910
Mom...

207
00:15:02,170 --> 00:15:04,110
Mom, don't go.

208
00:15:21,330 --> 00:15:22,430
Are you awake now?

209
00:15:25,060 --> 00:15:26,400
What happened?

210
00:15:28,800 --> 00:15:30,600
That's what I should be asking.

211
00:15:31,070 --> 00:15:32,240
Why did you do it?

212
00:15:32,740 --> 00:15:34,470
Why would you harm yourself?

213
00:15:36,510 --> 00:15:37,570
You said you were framed.

214
00:15:38,040 --> 00:15:39,640
You said you didn't do it.

215
00:15:40,340 --> 00:15:43,010
Then you have to live.
You have to live to clear your name.

216
00:15:46,380 --> 00:15:48,150
Do you have any water?

217
00:15:49,490 --> 00:15:51,920
Are you thirsty? Hold on.

218
00:16:03,730 --> 00:16:05,240
Thank you, Attorney Seo.

219
00:16:06,100 --> 00:16:08,140
Don't ever do that again.

220
00:16:09,710 --> 00:16:10,710
Okay.

221
00:16:11,340 --> 00:16:12,580
Never again.

222
00:16:17,180 --> 00:16:18,320
Is there enough for me?

223
00:16:18,720 --> 00:16:19,950
Look who didn't die.

224
00:16:48,110 --> 00:16:49,110
Mom.

225
00:16:49,910 --> 00:16:51,350
You're watching over me, right?

226
00:16:52,720 --> 00:16:54,750
I'll never disappoint you again.

227
00:16:55,820 --> 00:16:58,690
Even if the world locks me away,
I'll never give up.

228
00:16:59,490 --> 00:17:01,790
Whoever took your life
and did this to me,

229
00:17:02,290 --> 00:17:04,330
I'll find them and make them pay.

230
00:17:06,060 --> 00:17:07,700
So please, keep watching over me.

231
00:17:34,320 --> 00:17:37,330
(Care With Sincerity,
Guide With Integrity)

232
00:17:56,750 --> 00:18:01,320
(5 years later)

233
00:18:17,330 --> 00:18:18,540
(Korean Language)

234
00:18:23,510 --> 00:18:26,180
(High School Equivalency Test
Score Report)

235
00:18:26,240 --> 00:18:28,810
- Is that even possible?
- I've never seen that before.

236
00:18:28,810 --> 00:18:30,050
- That's amazing.
- No way.

237
00:18:30,050 --> 00:18:31,650
I see her in a different light now.

238
00:18:32,250 --> 00:18:33,420
Nobody saw this coming.

239
00:18:34,790 --> 00:18:36,520
She might get into college
at this rate.

240
00:18:36,720 --> 00:18:40,520
(Year 2022)

241
00:18:55,040 --> 00:18:57,170
Good work. You can go.

242
00:18:57,210 --> 00:18:58,310
Yes, ma'am.

243
00:19:05,120 --> 00:19:08,890
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation,
Chairman Kim Jung Sun)

244
00:19:09,220 --> 00:19:12,260
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation)

245
00:19:34,410 --> 00:19:37,650
I went and did a deep clean
of your office today, ma'am.

246
00:19:37,920 --> 00:19:39,780
I see. Good work.

247
00:19:39,780 --> 00:19:40,780
Thank you.

248
00:19:42,720 --> 00:19:45,590
So you're finally starting
at the office for real tomorrow?

249
00:19:46,320 --> 00:19:48,860
I can't just be
a figurehead chairman forever.

250
00:19:48,930 --> 00:19:51,430
The scholarship foundation
is Cheongma's largest shareholder.

251
00:19:51,730 --> 00:19:54,160
As chairman, I have to take on
some responsibility.

252
00:19:54,870 --> 00:19:57,230
You should've just stuck to acting.

253
00:19:57,300 --> 00:20:00,000
What'll you do
if you get in over your head?

254
00:20:00,800 --> 00:20:03,310
Why should I worry when I have you?

255
00:20:05,440 --> 00:20:09,280
So what's the first order
of business, Madam Chairman?

256
00:20:09,580 --> 00:20:12,980
I noticed the PR director position's
been vacant for a while.

257
00:20:13,380 --> 00:20:14,920
I plan on filling that role first.

258
00:20:14,950 --> 00:20:17,290
Right, the PR director.

259
00:20:17,450 --> 00:20:19,420
Can you think of anyone suitable?

260
00:20:20,420 --> 00:20:22,960
I'll have Chief Choi
recommend a few people.

261
00:20:30,070 --> 00:20:31,770
You want me to recommend you,
Manager Joo?

262
00:20:32,200 --> 00:20:35,170
If you do this for me,
I'll owe you one, Mr. Choi.

263
00:20:35,540 --> 00:20:36,770
Come on.

264
00:20:37,040 --> 00:20:39,440
You should just stick to handling
the CEO's family matters.

265
00:20:39,540 --> 00:20:40,940
Don't be greedy.

266
00:20:41,780 --> 00:20:43,280
Know your place.

267
00:20:53,120 --> 00:20:54,520
Hello? Hey, Hae Ra.

268
00:20:54,690 --> 00:20:56,790
I think I'm going to get expelled.

269
00:20:56,860 --> 00:20:57,860
What?

270
00:20:57,860 --> 00:21:00,760
What are you talking about?
Expelled? Why?

271
00:21:01,670 --> 00:21:04,200
There's an issue
with my graduation project.

272
00:21:04,700 --> 00:21:05,940
What kind of issue?

273
00:21:06,540 --> 00:21:07,900
It's nothing.

274
00:21:08,170 --> 00:21:09,910
Like they'd expel you over nothing.

275
00:21:10,140 --> 00:21:12,980
Whatever. Just fix this for me.

276
00:21:13,040 --> 00:21:14,380
This isn't Korea.

277
00:21:14,440 --> 00:21:16,150
How can I settle a matter in the US?

278
00:21:16,350 --> 00:21:17,480
Then what?

279
00:21:17,610 --> 00:21:19,620
Am I supposed to just get expelled
and humiliated?

280
00:21:19,720 --> 00:21:21,450
Humiliation's the least
of your worries.

281
00:21:21,650 --> 00:21:24,450
You think your father's going
to let this slide?

282
00:21:24,690 --> 00:21:26,260
Dad can't know about this,
of course.

283
00:21:31,160 --> 00:21:34,260
What did you say?
Hae Ra's getting expelled? Why?

284
00:21:35,170 --> 00:21:36,700
Looks like she got caught...

285
00:21:36,770 --> 00:21:38,800
plagiarizing a friend's design
for her graduation project.

286
00:21:39,500 --> 00:21:41,270
Honestly.

287
00:21:42,010 --> 00:21:44,710
Chief Choi, how did you find out?

288
00:21:45,440 --> 00:21:48,450
I was asked to verify her identity
before they ran the story.

289
00:21:48,910 --> 00:21:50,050
An article?

290
00:21:50,810 --> 00:21:53,050
So, did you block it
from coming out?

291
00:21:53,350 --> 00:21:55,690
Of course. I handled it.

292
00:21:58,790 --> 00:22:00,920
Get Hae Ra back to Korea right now.

293
00:22:06,260 --> 00:22:07,260
Hae Ra.

294
00:22:14,910 --> 00:22:16,670
Mom.

295
00:22:17,310 --> 00:22:19,040
Oh, honestly.

296
00:22:19,440 --> 00:22:21,910
I swear, you'll be the death of me.

297
00:22:22,410 --> 00:22:23,610
Is Dad home?

298
00:22:24,150 --> 00:22:25,380
Kang Hae Ra.

299
00:22:26,320 --> 00:22:28,890
What's wrong with you?

300
00:22:28,990 --> 00:22:30,950
I sent you to fashion school
to develop your skills,

301
00:22:31,020 --> 00:22:32,290
and you resort to stealing?

302
00:22:32,820 --> 00:22:35,290
Stealing? Come on.
It wasn't like that.

303
00:22:35,590 --> 00:22:38,960
If you stole your friend's design,
that's theft. Plain and simple.

304
00:22:40,560 --> 00:22:42,870
What would you have done
if they published the article?

305
00:22:43,330 --> 00:22:45,540
You said you stopped it, right?
So it's fine.

306
00:22:46,340 --> 00:22:47,470
Kang Hae Ra.

307
00:22:47,700 --> 00:22:48,940
Okay, I get it.

308
00:22:49,010 --> 00:22:50,940
I heard you, so drop it.

309
00:22:51,240 --> 00:22:52,680
I can't believe her.

310
00:22:52,740 --> 00:22:53,880
Get back here.

311
00:22:53,880 --> 00:22:56,180
Honey, that's enough.

312
00:22:56,280 --> 00:22:57,810
She said she heard you.

313
00:23:00,550 --> 00:23:02,390
- Darn.
- Unbelievable.

314
00:23:03,050 --> 00:23:05,020
You're sure you managed
to kill the story?

315
00:23:05,690 --> 00:23:07,820
Chief Choi said he stopped it,
so it must be true.

316
00:23:08,830 --> 00:23:09,830
My gosh.

317
00:23:10,360 --> 00:23:11,390
Ma'am.

318
00:23:13,460 --> 00:23:14,970
The PR director position...

319
00:23:15,400 --> 00:23:16,670
Have you filled it yet?

320
00:23:17,130 --> 00:23:18,340
No, not yet.

321
00:23:19,200 --> 00:23:20,400
But why do you ask?

322
00:23:21,300 --> 00:23:22,370
By any chance,

323
00:23:22,940 --> 00:23:25,010
are you interested in the position,
Manager Joo?

324
00:23:26,410 --> 00:23:29,510
If you give me the position,
I know I can do a great job.

325
00:23:31,950 --> 00:23:33,920
Of course you'd do well,
Manager Joo.

326
00:23:35,290 --> 00:23:37,920
Okay.
I'll discuss it with my husband.

327
00:23:38,790 --> 00:23:39,790
Thank you.

328
00:23:47,400 --> 00:23:48,730
Manager Joo said that?

329
00:23:49,070 --> 00:23:50,870
That she wants to be PR director
for the foundation?

330
00:23:51,200 --> 00:23:52,600
She didn't ask for it.

331
00:23:52,770 --> 00:23:54,970
She said she'd do a good job
if given the chance.

332
00:23:55,270 --> 00:23:58,840
That's the same thing, isn't it?
So what did you say?

333
00:24:00,110 --> 00:24:02,110
I said I'd discuss it with you.

334
00:24:02,950 --> 00:24:05,250
Should I tell her she can have
the PR director position?

335
00:24:06,320 --> 00:24:08,220
This isn't something
to decide hastily.

336
00:24:08,290 --> 00:24:09,850
Let's think about it some more.

337
00:24:11,320 --> 00:24:15,630
Fine, then you decide.
I'll be the one to tell her.

338
00:24:26,570 --> 00:24:29,840
I'm back in Korea.
So when are you coming back?

339
00:24:29,940 --> 00:24:32,280
What are you talking about?
I have to finish my studies first.

340
00:24:32,580 --> 00:24:34,210
But you're almost done with college.

341
00:24:34,440 --> 00:24:36,510
I told you. I'm going to get my MBA.

342
00:24:36,610 --> 00:24:38,680
That was the plan
when I was still in the US.

343
00:24:38,750 --> 00:24:40,520
Things are different now.

344
00:24:41,280 --> 00:24:43,320
I already discussed it
with CEO Kang.

345
00:24:43,790 --> 00:24:45,190
No one asked you to cause trouble.

346
00:24:48,120 --> 00:24:49,860
So you're just going to stay there?

347
00:24:50,390 --> 00:24:52,200
But I don't want
to be apart from you.

348
00:24:52,260 --> 00:24:54,400
We can call and text.
What's the issue?

349
00:24:56,770 --> 00:24:59,900
Then you have to call
and text me every day. Got it?

350
00:25:00,400 --> 00:25:02,340
I get it, okay? I'm hanging up now.

351
00:25:14,520 --> 00:25:16,120
(Ko Eun Seol)

352
00:25:18,290 --> 00:25:20,220
I'll call you every day, text you,

353
00:25:20,420 --> 00:25:21,760
and email you.

354
00:25:22,730 --> 00:25:25,300
I'll never forget you,
so promise me...

355
00:25:26,430 --> 00:25:27,960
you won't forget me either.

356
00:25:32,400 --> 00:25:33,870
Promise me, come on.

357
00:25:38,810 --> 00:25:39,910
You promised.

358
00:25:41,310 --> 00:25:42,980
We'll see each other again, okay?

359
00:25:49,420 --> 00:25:50,420
(Ko Eun Seol)

360
00:25:51,690 --> 00:25:54,460
The number you have dialed
is not in service.

361
00:25:54,860 --> 00:25:57,060
Please check the number
and try again.

362
00:26:00,730 --> 00:26:02,870
(Delete Contact)

363
00:26:08,540 --> 00:26:11,310
You call this handling it,
Chief Choi?

364
00:26:11,680 --> 00:26:12,980
I'm sorry, sir.

365
00:26:13,410 --> 00:26:15,250
They clearly promised
not to run the story...

366
00:26:15,310 --> 00:26:17,110
And you were naive enough
to believe them?

367
00:26:17,180 --> 00:26:19,350
Don't you know
what reporters are like?

368
00:26:21,990 --> 00:26:24,520
What are you going to do now that
the Korean press is all over this?

369
00:26:24,750 --> 00:26:26,420
Have you come up with a plan?

370
00:26:27,590 --> 00:26:29,860
I think the best move is
to face this head-on.

371
00:26:30,560 --> 00:26:32,660
Head-on? How?

372
00:26:33,760 --> 00:26:37,370
By having Hae Ra face the press
and publicly apologize.

373
00:26:38,300 --> 00:26:39,940
We can't do that, sir.

374
00:26:40,200 --> 00:26:42,470
Hae Ra will be the future owner
of Cheongma,

375
00:26:42,540 --> 00:26:44,980
and we can't afford any stain
on her reputation.

376
00:26:45,310 --> 00:26:47,140
That's right. I'm not doing it.

377
00:26:47,440 --> 00:26:50,280
A public apology?
That's beyond embarrassing.

378
00:26:50,780 --> 00:26:52,320
You, keep quiet.

379
00:26:52,380 --> 00:26:55,920
My gosh. It's not like
we have any other choice.

380
00:26:56,290 --> 00:26:58,920
What can we do when public opinion
is already in an uproar?

381
00:26:58,990 --> 00:27:00,560
We need to flip the narrative.

382
00:27:00,560 --> 00:27:02,690
- How?
- Hae Ra, you...

383
00:27:04,590 --> 00:27:07,260
Flip the narrative? How?

384
00:27:07,760 --> 00:27:10,570
I'll go to the US tomorrow morning
to take care of it,

385
00:27:10,770 --> 00:27:12,770
so please give me a few days.

386
00:27:14,600 --> 00:27:16,610
Manager Joo,
are you sure you can do this?

387
00:27:17,670 --> 00:27:18,680
Yes.

388
00:27:21,980 --> 00:27:23,210
Mom!

389
00:27:23,450 --> 00:27:25,680
What's all the fuss about?

390
00:27:25,680 --> 00:27:26,780
Look at this.

391
00:27:26,880 --> 00:27:28,550
I think Manager Joo
solved my problem.

392
00:27:28,550 --> 00:27:29,550
What?

393
00:27:31,690 --> 00:27:36,260
"A scandal fueled by xenophobia
and bias against the wealthy?"

394
00:27:36,890 --> 00:27:38,130
Slick, right?

395
00:27:39,060 --> 00:27:40,200
Quiet down a second.

396
00:27:40,960 --> 00:27:43,000
"Recently, the industry..."

397
00:27:43,000 --> 00:27:45,070
Wait. My goodness.

398
00:27:46,670 --> 00:27:47,970
No way.

399
00:27:48,670 --> 00:27:50,440
Good work, Manager Joo.

400
00:27:51,570 --> 00:27:52,810
Thank you, sir.

401
00:27:53,910 --> 00:27:57,010
How did you convince the victim
to give that kind of interview?

402
00:27:57,210 --> 00:27:59,380
You didn't bribe her with money,
did you?

403
00:28:00,880 --> 00:28:02,320
Do you think I'd risk that?

404
00:28:03,290 --> 00:28:04,490
Besides, after meeting her,

405
00:28:04,550 --> 00:28:06,820
I could tell
money won't buy her off.

406
00:28:07,060 --> 00:28:09,930
Then, how did you persuade her?

407
00:28:11,060 --> 00:28:12,530
Turns out she's pretty ambitious.

408
00:28:13,260 --> 00:28:16,500
I promised her a collaboration
with Cheongma Fashion.

409
00:28:16,500 --> 00:28:18,700
How is that any different
from bribing her?

410
00:28:19,440 --> 00:28:20,540
Well, it is.

411
00:28:21,070 --> 00:28:22,970
I simply recognized her ambition.

412
00:28:23,640 --> 00:28:27,480
And I don't believe my proposal
will hurt Cheongma in any way.

413
00:28:28,240 --> 00:28:30,810
Still, how could you make
a call like that on your own?

414
00:28:30,810 --> 00:28:33,950
Well, don't worry about that.
I gave her full authority.

415
00:28:35,450 --> 00:28:36,450
Understood.

416
00:28:38,620 --> 00:28:40,190
Chief Choi, you can go now.

417
00:28:42,130 --> 00:28:43,130
Yes, sir.

418
00:28:48,470 --> 00:28:50,030
Manager Joo, have a seat.

419
00:28:56,940 --> 00:29:00,010
Word is you're interested in
the foundation's PR director role.

420
00:29:02,650 --> 00:29:04,610
I want you to take it.

421
00:29:05,250 --> 00:29:07,080
Given how you handled
this situation,

422
00:29:07,080 --> 00:29:08,450
I know I can trust you with it.

423
00:29:10,150 --> 00:29:11,620
Thank you, sir.

424
00:29:12,260 --> 00:29:15,260
I'll work hard
not to disappoint you.

425
00:29:21,830 --> 00:29:25,470
(Year 2026)

426
00:29:33,610 --> 00:29:35,750
Hey, that's enough. You can stop.

427
00:29:39,050 --> 00:29:41,120
Hey, my shoulders are next.

428
00:29:44,650 --> 00:29:48,060
What the...
You did that on purpose, didn't you?

429
00:29:48,690 --> 00:29:49,760
Why you...

430
00:29:50,190 --> 00:29:51,190
Darn.

431
00:29:52,130 --> 00:29:53,130
What gives?

432
00:29:53,300 --> 00:29:54,660
We don't do violence here.

433
00:29:55,830 --> 00:29:56,830
What?

434
00:29:57,700 --> 00:29:59,400
Hey, let go.

435
00:30:02,510 --> 00:30:04,440
Hey! Okay, I get it, so let go.

436
00:30:06,080 --> 00:30:07,310
Darn it.

437
00:30:10,080 --> 00:30:11,080
Thanks.

438
00:30:11,680 --> 00:30:13,320
Inmate 2751, visitor.

439
00:30:15,050 --> 00:30:16,050
I have good news.

440
00:30:17,590 --> 00:30:18,620
Good news?

441
00:30:19,060 --> 00:30:21,760
- What...
- It's been a tough ten years.

442
00:30:22,960 --> 00:30:24,730
Your parole was approved.

443
00:30:25,200 --> 00:30:26,300
Parole?

444
00:30:27,260 --> 00:30:28,970
Does that mean I'm getting out?

445
00:30:28,970 --> 00:30:30,600
Yes, soon.

446
00:30:32,240 --> 00:30:34,970
Thank you.
Thank you so much, Attorney Seo.

447
00:30:36,110 --> 00:30:39,240
You don't have to thank me.
This was all you.

448
00:30:43,080 --> 00:30:45,180
(Building
Advanced Constitutional State...)

449
00:30:45,180 --> 00:30:47,250
(Where People Are Happy)

450
00:31:03,570 --> 00:31:05,000
The real work starts now.

451
00:31:34,230 --> 00:31:38,100
(A Trap Called Desire)

452
00:31:38,300 --> 00:31:40,240
Who was released? Find out.

453
00:31:40,300 --> 00:31:43,070
There was a man named Lee Jung Tae
who worked here ten years ago.

454
00:31:43,570 --> 00:31:45,240
It's not like I chose to fail,
you know.

455
00:31:45,510 --> 00:31:47,880
Maybe I can use this to get them
to set up my marriage to Seok Jin.

456
00:31:47,880 --> 00:31:50,380
Taking one step back
to take two steps forward.

457
00:31:50,380 --> 00:31:52,920
The nerve of her. She's only been
at this for a few years.

458
00:31:52,980 --> 00:31:55,320
Don't forget you started out
as a nanny, Director Joo.

459
00:31:55,450 --> 00:31:57,120
Wasn't she convicted of murder?

460
00:31:57,220 --> 00:31:59,960
Why would you invite her to stay
when we have Teun Teun here?

461
00:31:59,960 --> 00:32:01,820
Eun Seol didn't do it, Mom.

462
00:32:01,820 --> 00:32:03,130
If she didn't do it,

463
00:32:03,190 --> 00:32:05,230
then why did she rot in prison
for ten years?

464
00:32:05,230 --> 00:32:06,700
Who says I'm your brother?

465
00:32:06,700 --> 00:32:08,560
If I see you one more time,

466
00:32:08,630 --> 00:32:10,070
you're dead.

467
00:32:10,830 --> 00:32:12,840
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
